# Android 17 vold only talks to the AIDL IBootControl; legacy vendors (9 Pro:
# android.hardware.boot@1.1 HIDL) are refused ("IBootControl HIDL versions 1.1
# and earlier are no longer supported"), so no boot is ever marked successful
# and the bootloader marks the slot unbootable after 7 boots.
# bootctl_hidl (KernelSU's HIDL bootctl) marks it once the boot completed.
on property:sys.boot_completed=1
    exec_background - root root -- /system/bin/bootctl_hidl mark-boot-successful
